  "raw": {
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/manager-analytics-capability-data-delivery-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery",
      "description": "Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery 496091 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 4 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Bring your data and analytics leadership to JCU and make your mark in a newly created senior role. You’ll lead talented technical professionals, strengthen JCU’s enterprise data capability and help build the foundations for our future analytics and AI ambitions, with your work supporting better decision-making across the University. Full-time, continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas Attractive competitive remuneration package plus up to 17% employer superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE This role offers an exciting opportunity to help shape how JCU uses data to support better decision-making. You’ll have the opportunity to influence the development of JCU’s data capability, helping turn complex information into meaningful organisational insight and building solutions that respond to the evolving needs of the University. Working across JCU, you’ll bring together technology, people and business priorities to deliver practical, future-focused solutions. You’ll lead a multidisciplinary data engineering team, build strong partnerships across the University and have genuine scope to shape the future direction of JCU’s data, analytics and AI capability. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You’re an experienced data and analytics professional who can see the bigger picture while still understanding what it takes to deliver technically complex solutions. You’ll bring strong experience across business intelligence, data warehousing, enterprise databases and data pipelines, along with the ability to navigate complex environments and turn business needs into practical solutions. You’ll be confident building relationships across a large organisation, explaining complex technical concepts clearly and influencing decisions at different levels. As a leader, you’ll enjoy developing people and creating an environment where technical expertise, new ideas and collaboration can thrive. You’ll bring curiosity, sound judgement and advanced problem-solving skills, with the confidence to work through ambiguity, lead complex projects and provide clear, well-considered advice. You’ll also hold a relevant postgraduate qualification, be progressing towards one, or bring an equivalent combination of relevant education and experience. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Daniel Zamykal at daniel.zamykal@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your specialist anatomy expertise to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across human anatomy, and veterinary anatomy and necropsy. Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) Cairns Professional, Technical Bring your advanced technical expertise to JCU, providing coordination, advice and practical delivery to ensure safe, consistent and high-quality practical learning and teaching experiences across education, life and environmental sciences. Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology Cairns Academic Advance solutions to some of the Tropics’ most pressing land and water challenges. Join James Cook University as a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Environmental Hydrology and build impactful research, inspire future environmental scientists, and collaborate with industry, government and community partners to create real-world environmental outcomes. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/educational-technology-designer-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Educational Technology Designer",
      "description": "Educational Technology Designer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Educational Technology Designer 495859 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 8 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Join JCU's Graduate Research School on a 2-year fixed-term opportunity and help shape the future of researcher development. You'll design engaging online learning, collaborate with subject matter experts and apply emerging technologies to create accessible, high-quality professional development experiences that support HDR candidates and researchers across the University. Full-time, fixed-term opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 7: $99,878.44 - $110,446.52 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As the Educational Technology Designer , you will play a key role in enhancing research capability across JCU by creating engaging, accessible and scalable online professional development. You'll transform priority face-to-face offerings into high-quality digital learning experiences and help shape a contemporary professional development program that supports researchers and research students across the University. Working closely with academic and professional colleagues, subject matter experts and Colleges, you will design and maintain online learning modules, apply emerging technologies, and use learner insights to continuously improve outcomes. This is an opportunity to influence future learning design practices, support innovation in researcher development, and make a lasting impact across JCU WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE We are looking for a creative and collaborative learning design professional with qualifications and/or experience in instructional design, educational technology or a related field. You enjoy creating engaging online learning experiences and can confidently use learning management systems, authoring tools and multimedia technologies to develop accessible, high-quality learning resources. You have a talent for working with subject matter experts and translating complex concepts into clear, engaging and pedagogically sound learning experiences. With an understanding of the higher education environment and the needs of researchers and research students, you are committed to creating inclusive, accessible and equitable learning opportunities. You are comfortable exploring emerging technologies and can apply generative AI and other educational technologies in a responsible and ethical way. Coupled with strong analytical, organisational and problem-solving skills, you can manage competing priorities, establish effective processes and continuously improve learning outcomes and the overall learner experience. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Gabby Ryan at gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your specialist anatomy expertise to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across human anatomy, and veterinary anatomy and necropsy. Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) Cairns Professional, Technical Bring your advanced technical expertise to JCU, providing coordination, advice and practical delivery to ensure safe, consistent and high-quality practical learning and teaching experiences across education, life and environmental sciences. Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery Townsville Professional Lead the delivery of trusted enterprise data and analytics capabilities at JCU. Shape scalable platforms, strengthen AI readiness and guide a multidisciplinary team to deliver secure, reliable and cost-effective data solutions that inform strategic decision-making across the University. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
