    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-senior-lecturer-environmental-hydrology-cairns-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology",
      "description": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Lecturer / Senior Lecturer, Environmental Hydrology 496038 Cairns Academic Full time Closing on: Nov 24 2026 Position Description Full-time 36.25 hours per week | Continuing Appointment Based in Cairns Academic Level B $112,810 - $133,110 | Academic Level C $137,166 - $157,465 17% Super, 5 weeks annual leave, leave loading plus other great benefits Build an internationally competitive research program addressing contemporary environmental challenges. Inspire the next generation of environmental scientists through practical, field-based learning. Collaborate with Traditional Owners, government, industry, communities and research partners. Advance understanding of tropical catchments, landscapes and land–water systems. James Cook University (JCU) is seeking an emerging or established academic with expertise in environmental hydrology to join our College of Science and Engineering in Cairns. This is an opportunity to shape teaching and research in catchment hydrology and soil–water–vegetation interactions while contributing to JCU’s established strengths in tropical land and water systems. Your work will connect scientific understanding with practical environmental management, particularly in northern Australia and tropical environments. About the role As a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Environmental Hydrology, you will deliver engaging undergraduate and postgraduate teaching while developing a high-quality, internationally competitive research program. You will contribute to teaching across Environmental Science and Management, Science and Environment programs, including lectures, practical classes, field-based learning and assessment. You will also supervise undergraduate, postgraduate and higher degree by research students, helping them develop the knowledge and practical capability to address complex environmental challenges. Your research will strengthen understanding of environmental and hydrological processes, with opportunities to explore areas such as catchment hydrology, soil–water–vegetation interactions, water resources management, agricultural practice, water quality and climate adaptation. Working across disciplines, you will build productive partnerships with Traditional Owners, government agencies, industry, community organisations, non-government organisations and research collaborators in Australia and internationally. Key responsibilities In this role, you will: Deliver and coordinate high-quality teaching in environmental hydrology, land and water science, and related disciplines. Develop an impactful research program in environmental science and hydrological processes. Pursue competitive research funding and contribute to multidisciplinary research initiatives. Establish collaborative teaching and research partnerships in northern Australia, nationally and internationally. Supervise undergraduate research, Honours, postgraduate and higher degree by research students. Engage with Traditional Owners, government, industry, community organisations and research partners. Strengthen JCU’s visibility and reputation through professional engagement and public outreach. Contribute positively to the academic and collegiate life of the College. About you You will hold, or be close to completing, a PhD in environmental hydrology, environmental science, earth science, physical geography or a related discipline, supported by expertise in catchment processes. You will bring: Research expertise in environmental science and hydrological processes, including catchment hydrology or soil–water–vegetation interactions. A record of high-quality research publications relative to your career stage and opportunities. The capability to develop an independent, competitive and collaborative research program. A commitment to delivering engaging, inclusive and high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching. Experience or demonstrated potential in supervising undergraduate, postgraduate or higher degree by research students. The ability to plan and deliver research, teaching and field-based activities within multidisciplinary teams. The ability to communicate scientific information effectively to specialist and non-specialist audiences. A commitment to diversity, reconciliation and an inclusive working and learning environment. Experience in tropical or northern Australian environments, field-based teaching, quantitative analysis, spatial analysis or integrated catchment modelling will be highly regarded. We also welcome experience developing applied research partnerships or co-designing research with Traditional Owners, government, industry, non-government organisations or community groups. Why work at JCU? At JCU, your teaching and research can contribute directly to the environmental resilience and sustainable management of tropical landscapes and communities. Based in Cairns, you will work in a region that provides an exceptional setting for environmental teaching, field-based learning and applied research. You will join a collaborative academic community with opportunities to build interdisciplinary partnerships and connect your research with practical environmental challenges. JCU employees also enjoy a range of benefits, including: Five weeks’ annual leave plus leave loading. Flexible working arrangements. Up to 12 months’ paid parental leave. Salary packaging options. Paid study leave and staff development opportunities. Fitness Passport and health insurance discounts. A free Employee Assistance Program offering confidential coaching and counselling. Thinking of applying? We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. We also welcome applications from candidates in the final stages of their PhD who are interested in structured mentoring pathways. If you do not meet every listed criterion, we still encourage you to apply and demonstrate your potential. JCU recognises that career pathways and opportunities differ. The selection panel will consider your achievements, potential and performance relative to the opportunities available to you. If you require assistance preparing your application or adjustments during the recruitment process, please let us know so we can support your participation. How to apply Click Apply and: Complete the online application form. Upload your current résumé. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience against the key requirements and how your skills will support your success in the role. Join JCU and use your expertise in environmental hydrology to inspire students, advance tropical research and help address some of the most important land and water challenges facing northern Australia and the Tropics. For further information please contact Professor Alana Grech on (07) 4781 4107 or via email alana.grech@jcu.edu.au Recommended for you Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your specialist anatomy expertise to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across human anatomy, and veterinary anatomy and necropsy. Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) Cairns Professional, Technical Bring your advanced technical expertise to JCU, providing coordination, advice and practical delivery to ensure safe, consistent and high-quality practical learning and teaching experiences across education, life and environmental sciences. Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery Townsville Professional Lead the delivery of trusted enterprise data and analytics capabilities at JCU. Shape scalable platforms, strengthen AI readiness and guide a multidisciplinary team to deliver secure, reliable and cost-effective data solutions that inform strategic decision-making across the University. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/hdr-program-support-officer-townsville-qld-australia-8ad7ef9f-95c9-46e6-8bb0-5d9b6d3fa73b": {
      "title": "HDR Program Support Officer",
      "description": "HDR Program Support Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! HDR Program Support Officer 496063 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 8 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Join JCU's Graduate Research School and play an important role in supporting the next generation of researchers. Working closely with Higher Degree by Research (HDR) candidates, academic supervisors and University stakeholders, you will provide specialist administrative support across the research journey, helping students successfully navigate candidature milestones from admission through to completion. In this rewarding and varied role, you'll combine customer service, organisation and problem-solving skills to deliver a positive experience for our research community. Full-time, continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 5: $78,740.99 - $89,310.33 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As the HDR Program Support Officer, you will be a key contact for Higher Degree by Research candidates and supervisors, helping students navigate important candidature through every stage of their research journey. Working within the Graduate Research School, you will provide specialist administrative support, ensure important milestones stay on track and contribute to a positive experience for JCU's research community. You will collaborate with academic and professional staff across the University to support committee activities, respond to enquiries and contribute to continuous improvements that enhance the HDR candidate experience WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring knowledge of HDR candidature management, including enrolment, progression and completion requirements, together with an understanding of the importance of accuracy, policy compliance and attention to detail. With strong written and interpersonal communication skills, you will be comfortable assisting people from varied backgrounds and managing a high volume of enquiries. You will use sound judgement and problem-solving skills to provide clear information about processes and procedures, supported by confidence using Microsoft applications, databases and other computerised systems. Well organised and responsive, you will be able to balance competing deadlines, work independently and contribute positively as part of a collaborative team. You will also hold qualifications and experience appropriate to the requirements of the role. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville campus Eligibility: Please note that current students are not eligible to apply for this position. HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Please note that current students are not eligible to apply for this position. Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Gabby Ryan at gabby.ryan@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your specialist anatomy expertise to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across human anatomy, and veterinary anatomy and necropsy. Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) Cairns Professional, Technical Bring your advanced technical expertise to JCU, providing coordination, advice and practical delivery to ensure safe, consistent and high-quality practical learning and teaching experiences across education, life and environmental sciences. Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery Townsville Professional Lead the delivery of trusted enterprise data and analytics capabilities at JCU. Shape scalable platforms, strengthen AI readiness and guide a multidisciplinary team to deliver secure, reliable and cost-effective data solutions that inform strategic decision-making across the University. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
