    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/scheduling-services-officer-townsville-qld-australia-321e576f-08f6-40e8-b9d6-6f415d145c52": {
      "title": "Scheduling Services Officer",
      "description": "Scheduling Services Officer - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Scheduling Services Officer 496019 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 8 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. We are seeking two organised and solutions-focused Scheduling Services Officers to join JCU on a fixed-term basis, bringing their scheduling, coordination and customer service expertise to deliver accurate, integrated timetable and class registration support across the University. One full-time, fixed-term opportunity until August 2027 | 36.25 hours per week One full-time, fixed-term opportunity until January 2028 | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas HEWL 5: $78,740 - $89,310 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE In this fast-paced and customer-focused role, you will contribute to the development, publication and ongoing maintenance of the University timetable, alongside student class registration and room booking services within a complex operating environment. Working as a partner to allocated academic areas, you will build strong stakeholder relationships, coordinate and prioritise competing scheduling requirements, and use specialist scheduling systems to deliver accurate, responsive and high-quality services that meet the needs of staff and students. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring demonstrated scheduling and coordination experience, including the effective allocation of resources and delivery of outcomes in a systematic and organised manner. You will have strong organisational, administrative, problem-solving and critical-thinking skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. Highly developed communication and interpersonal skills will enable you to build effective stakeholder relationships, manage expectations, negotiate competing needs and navigate challenging situations. You will also have effective computer and data-entry skills, experience with Microsoft Office, and the ability to confidently learn and use specialist scheduling systems. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Jenna Tolcher at jenna.tolcher@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your specialist anatomy expertise to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across human anatomy, and veterinary anatomy and necropsy. Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) Cairns Professional, Technical Bring your advanced technical expertise to JCU, providing coordination, advice and practical delivery to ensure safe, consistent and high-quality practical learning and teaching experiences across education, life and environmental sciences. Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery Townsville Professional Lead the delivery of trusted enterprise data and analytics capabilities at JCU. Shape scalable platforms, strengthen AI readiness and guide a multidisciplinary team to deliver secure, reliable and cost-effective data solutions that inform strategic decision-making across the University. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
