    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/manager-laboratory-and-technical-services-aithm-cairns-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services, AITHM",
      "description": "Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services, AITHM - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Manager, Laboratory and Technical Services, AITHM 496057 Cairns Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 8 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Ready to lead the laboratory and technical services and manage the specialised infrastructure that enables world-leading tropical health research? Join the Australian Institute of Tropical Health and Medicine (AITHM) and work alongside researchers tackling some of the most significant health challenges facing tropical regions. You'll empower a skilled technical workforce, shape the future of research support services and help create the environment where discovery and innovation thrive. Full-time, continuing opportunity | 36.25 hours per week Based at the Cairns Nguma-bada campus, Smithfield HEWL 8: $111,960 - $128,567 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE In this influential leadership role, you will provide direction across laboratory and technical services, ensuring researchers have access to high-quality facilities, specialist equipment and expert support. AITHM's research infrastructure includes specialised facilities such as PC2 and PC3 laboratories, mosquito insectaries, and other research environments supporting tropical health and infectious disease research. Working closely with stakeholders across the Institute, you will oversee laboratory operations, resource allocation, governance, safety and compliance while leading a team of technical professionals. You will play a key role in driving service improvements, enhancing operational effectiveness and ensuring laboratory and technical services remain responsive to the evolving needs of research programs. Through strong leadership and strategic planning, you will foster a culture of collaboration, accountability and continuous improvement while supporting the delivery of world-class tropical health and medical research. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You are an experienced leader with a strong background in laboratory operations, technical services or research support environments. You bring demonstrated success leading teams, managing operational resources and delivering effective, high-quality technical and research support services within complex organisations. Your understanding of laboratory governance, compliance and workplace health and safety enables you to confidently manage risk while maintaining high operational standards. Coupled with excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills, you can build productive relationships, influence outcomes and support a positive, high-performing workplace culture. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Alex Loukas at directoraithm@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your specialist anatomy expertise to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across human anatomy, and veterinary anatomy and necropsy. Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) Cairns Professional, Technical Bring your advanced technical expertise to JCU, providing coordination, advice and practical delivery to ensure safe, consistent and high-quality practical learning and teaching experiences across education, life and environmental sciences. Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery Townsville Professional Lead the delivery of trusted enterprise data and analytics capabilities at JCU. Shape scalable platforms, strengthen AI readiness and guide a multidisciplinary team to deliver secure, reliable and cost-effective data solutions that inform strategic decision-making across the University. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
