    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/strategic-asset-planner-townsville-qld-australia-5ef6ddae-8ae1-4aa7-915a-35cbd2cee864": {
      "title": "Strategic Asset Planner",
      "description": "Strategic Asset Planner - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Strategic Asset Planner 496020 Townsville Professional Full time Closing on: Nov 5 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Are you an ambitious and skilled Strategic Asset Planner ready for your next challenge? This is an exciting opportunity to lead JCU's asset planning, maintenance and replacement programs, influencing key investment decisions and driving asset performance, sustainability and compliance across a unique and diverse university estate. The position is full-time, on a continuing basis and based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, Douglas. HEWL 8: $111,960 - $128,567 per annum plus up to 17% employer superannuation contributions. ABOUT THE ROLE The Strategic Asset Planner leads the University's asset planning, maintenance and replacement programs in alignment with the Strategic Asset Management Framework and Estate Directorate maintenance strategy. The role delivers risk-informed asset planning and investment prioritisation that strengthens asset performance, sustainability and compliance outcomes across the University's built and natural environment. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will be a strategic and analytical asset management professional with experience delivering asset planning, maintenance and renewal programs within complex environments. You will bring qualifications and/or demonstrated experience in asset management, engineering, facilities management or a related discipline, together with a strong understanding of strategic asset management frameworks, lifecycle planning and risk-based investment decision-making. You will have the ability to develop and implement planned maintenance and asset replacement programs, using data, technical information and financial insights to inform practical and sustainable asset strategies. You will also bring strong leadership capability, with the ability to influence outcomes, build productive relationships and work effectively with technical, operational and corporate stakeholders. You will balance competing priorities and drive continuous improvement initiatives that enhance asset performance, service delivery and organisational outcomes. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave Flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Townsville and Cairns’ campuses HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the key requirements of the role and how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Daniel Nixon at daniel.nixon@jcu.edu.au ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your specialist anatomy expertise to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across human anatomy, and veterinary anatomy and necropsy. Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) Cairns Professional, Technical Bring your advanced technical expertise to JCU, providing coordination, advice and practical delivery to ensure safe, consistent and high-quality practical learning and teaching experiences across education, life and environmental sciences. Manager, Analytics Capability & Data Delivery Townsville Professional Lead the delivery of trusted enterprise data and analytics capabilities at JCU. Shape scalable platforms, strengthen AI readiness and guide a multidisciplinary team to deliver secure, reliable and cost-effective data solutions that inform strategic decision-making across the University. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
