    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/clinical-educator-lecturer-occupational-therapy-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Clinical Educator / Lecturer, Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Clinical Educator / Lecturer, Occupational Therapy - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Clinical Educator / Lecturer, Occupational Therapy 496090 Townsville Academic Full time Closing on: Nov 18 2026 Position Description Fixed term contract to cover parental leave to September 2027. Full time(36.25 hours per week) Academic Level B $112,810 - $133,110 + 17% Super Based at the JCU Clinical Practices Building on the Townsville (Bebegu Yumba) campus. Shape the next generation of occupational therapists through hands-on clinical education Support meaningful, student-led occupational therapy services for children, young people and families Join a collaborative team committed to interdisciplinary learning and improving access to care in North Queensland James Cook University is seeking an experienced and enthusiastic occupational therapist to join our team as a Clinical Educator/Lecturer, Occupational Therapy. This is an exciting opportunity to combine your clinical expertise with your passion for education. You will supervise and support occupational therapy students as they gain valuable practical experience while delivering meaningful services to children, young people, families and the wider community. About the role Based within JCU’s student-led occupational therapy service, you will provide clinical education, supervision and support for undergraduate occupational therapy students undertaking observational and block placements. The service primarily supports children and young people aged 18 months to 18 years who may otherwise experience difficulty accessing occupational therapy in the local community. Depending on individual needs, services may include assessment, therapy, home or school programs, group sessions and collaboration with families, schools, health professionals and other service providers. You will also contribute to interdisciplinary programs for adults and children and help shape the continued development of JCU’s occupational therapy service. Key responsibilities In this varied and rewarding role, you will: Educate, supervise, support and evaluate undergraduate occupational therapy students undertaking clinical placements Guide students in the assessment and delivery of therapy for children with developmental delays, learning difficulties, motor challenges and sensory processing needs Support a family-centred approach through consultation and collaboration with families, teachers, health professionals and other key stakeholders Facilitate student involvement in interdisciplinary therapy programs and group activities Ensure the completion of timely, accurate and professional clinical documentation, including file notes, reports, home programs and correspondence Coordinate client appointments, follow-up activities and other administrative requirements Contribute to the ongoing development of the occupational therapy service, with a focus on strengthening interdisciplinary practice Participate in relevant University activities and meetings About you You are a collaborative and engaging occupational therapist who enjoys helping students translate academic learning into confident, professional practice. You will bring: A degree qualification, or higher, in Occupational Therapy from a World Federation of Occupational Therapists accredited university Current registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency or eligibility to obtain registration Demonstrated clinical experience working with paediatric clients Experience educating and supervising undergraduate occupational therapy students The ability to promote collaborative and interdisciplinary learning Strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills Well-developed organisational and time-management capabilities The ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team Experience in health-related research or consultancy, or occupational therapy practice and education in rural, regional or remote settings, will be highly regarded. Why work at JCU? At JCU, you will be part of a purpose-driven university focused on creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond. This role offers the opportunity to make a genuine difference by supporting student development, strengthening clinical education and improving access to occupational therapy services within the North Queensland community. JCU employees also enjoy a range of benefits, including: Five weeks annual leave plus leave loading Up to 12 months paid parental leave Flexible work arrangements Salary packaging options Paid study leave and staff development opportunities Fitness Passport and health insurance discounts Free Employee Assistance Program, including confidential coaching and counselling How to apply Click the Apply button and complete the online application form. Please upload: Your current resume A cover letter outlining your relevant clinical and educational experience and how your skills will contribute to your success in this role Join JCU and use your clinical expertise to inspire future occupational therapists while supporting children, young people and families across North Queensland. For further information, please contact Dr Dan Lowrie on (07) 4781 5951 or via email daniel.lowrie@jcu.edu.au Recommended for you Technical Officer (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your laboratory and technical skills to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality learning and teaching across human and veterinary anatomy and pathology. Senior Lecturer, Adult Health Townsville Academic Bring your surgical expertise and passion for medical education to JCU, where you’ll shape clinical learning, inspire future doctors and strengthen healthcare across regional Australia. Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor, Townsville Clinical School Townsville Academic Shape the future of medical education in northern Australia. Join JCU as Associate Professor, Townsville Clinical School and provide academic leadership that strengthens clinical education, student success and the future regional medical workforce. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-associate-professor-townsville-clinical-school-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor, Townsville Clinical School",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor, Townsville Clinical School - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Senior Lecturer / Associate Professor, Townsville Clinical School 496088 Townsville Academic Part time Closing on: Nov 10 2026 Position Description 0.2 FTE - 7.25 hours per week | Continuing Appointment Academic Level C $137,166 - $157,465 Academic Level D $164,231 - $180,463 Based in Townsville Provide senior academic leadership within the Townsville Clinical School Shape high-quality clinical education across the clinical years of JCU’s MBBS program Strengthen partnerships that support regional, rural and remote health workforce development Contribute to student success, educational innovation and socially accountable medical education Join a university committed to improving health outcomes across northern Australia James Cook University is seeking an experienced clinician and medical educator to join the Townsville Clinical School as a Senior Lecturer or Associate Professor. This is an opportunity to use your clinical expertise and educational leadership to influence the quality and future direction of medical education at JCU. Working closely with the Head of Clinical School, you will help create high-quality clinical learning experiences that prepare students for professional practice and support the future medical workforce of northern Australia. About the role You will provide senior academic leadership and contribute to the delivery, quality and continual improvement of JCU’s MBBS program, with a particular focus on students completing the clinical years of the program. You will work collaboratively with academic staff, clinicians, health services, clinical educators and community partners to support teaching, assessment, curriculum delivery, student development and academic quality. You will also help strengthen clinical learning opportunities across hospital, community, primary care and rural healthcare settings. This influential role offers the opportunity to advance medical education, guide clinical educators and contribute to educational innovation and scholarship with meaningful regional impact. Key responsibilities In this role, you will: Provide senior academic leadership in support of the Head of Clinical School. Coordinate and contribute to clinical teaching, assessment, mentoring and student learning across the MBBS program. Support curriculum delivery, assessment design, academic standards, quality assurance and continuous improvement. Promote student success, wellbeing, professionalism and professional identity formation. Build productive partnerships with health services, clinicians, general practice networks, private healthcare providers, rural placement sites and community partners. Provide leadership, mentoring and support to clinical educators, preceptors, adjunct academics and other teaching staff. Contribute to scholarship, research and educational innovation in medical education, clinical training and health workforce development. Participate in academic governance, planning and initiatives that support the Townsville Clinical School and broader MBBS program. About you You are an accomplished clinician and medical educator with the credibility, leadership capability and collaborative approach to positively influence medical education and clinical training. You will bring: A postgraduate qualification and significant clinical experience within the Australian health system or an equivalent healthcare environment. Extensive experience in teaching, assessment and curriculum development in undergraduate or postgraduate medical education. Demonstrated leadership in medical education, clinical service, professional practice or health workforce development. Experience contributing to curriculum innovation, assessment development, quality assurance and continuous improvement. The ability to communicate with influence, shape strategic thinking and build productive relationships across academic, clinical and community settings. Experience contributing to academic governance, educational policy and the maintenance of academic standards. A record of contribution to scholarship, research, professional practice or educational innovation. An understanding of how medical education supports rural, regional, remote and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander health workforce development. Why work at JCU At JCU, you will be part of a university with a clear purpose: creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond through education and research that makes a difference. The College of Medicine and Dentistry is committed to strengthening healthcare across northern Australia through socially accountable education, discovery, advocacy, partnerships and leadership. You will join a collaborative academic community focused on preparing health professionals to make a meaningful contribution in rural, regional and underserved communities. JCU employees can also access a range of benefits, including: Five weeks annual leave plus leave loading Flexible work arrangements Up to 12 months paid parental leave Salary packaging options Paid study leave and staff development programs Fitness Passport and health insurance discounts Free Employee Assistance Program, including coaching and counselling How to apply Click the Apply button and complete the online application form. Alternatively, visit the JCU Careers page and search for the position. Please upload: Your current resume A cover letter outlining your relevant experience against the key requirements of the role and how your capabilities will support your success in the position Bring your clinical and educational leadership to JCU and help shape the next generation of doctors serving northern Australia. For more information about the position, please contact David Belstead on (07) 4781 4046 or via email david.belstead@jcu.edu.au Recommended for you Technical Officer (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your laboratory and technical skills to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality learning and teaching across human and veterinary anatomy and pathology. Senior Lecturer, Adult Health Townsville Academic Bring your surgical expertise and passion for medical education to JCU, where you’ll shape clinical learning, inspire future doctors and strengthen healthcare across regional Australia. Clinical Educator / Lecturer, Occupational Therapy Townsville Academic Combine your passion for occupational therapy and clinical education in a rewarding role where you’ll shape the next generation of OTs while making a meaningful difference for children, young people and families in North Queensland. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/technical-advisor-anatomy-and-pathology-townsville-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology)",
      "description": "Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) - Townsville, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) 496132 Townsville Professional Technical Full time Closing on: Nov 17 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Are you an experienced technical professional with expertise in anatomy, pathology or related laboratory environments? Join JCU and contribute your specialist skills to the delivery of high-quality practical learning and teaching across Human Anatomy, and Veterinary Anatomy and Pathology. We are seeking three experienced Technical Advisors (Anatomy and Pathology) to provide specialist scientific and technical support across our multiple anatomy and pathology teaching environments. Laboratory and Technical Services, Education Division Three full-time positions available Full-time, continuing | 36.25 hours per week Successful candidate must be based in Townsville or willing to relocate before commencement Based at the Townsville Bebegu Yumba campus, gateway to the Great Barrier Reef and tropical North Queensland HEWL 6: $90,821 - $98,369 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation Relocation Assistance may be considered for the ideal candidate ABOUT THE ROLE As a Technical Advisor (Anatomy and Pathology) , you will bring your specialist knowledge and hands-on technical expertise to facilitate high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate learning and teaching. You will prepare laboratories, equipment, specimens and teaching resources for practical classes, intensives, workshops and other learning experiences, ensuring activities are safe, effective and specimens are ready for learning and teaching delivery. We currently have three full-time positions available, with staff providing technical services in specialised laboratories across multiple discipline areas, including Human Anatomy, and Veterinary Anatomy and Pathology. Depending on operational requirements, you will work with human and/or animal anatomical specimens, undertaking activities such as specimen preparation and preservation, embalming, dissection and prosection, as well as practical set ups, safe handling, storage and management of cadaveric resources. You will also contribute to the day-to-day operation of anatomy and pathology facilities, including equipment maintenance and troubleshooting, biosafety and biosecurity control, procurement and asset management, and liaison with suppliers and contractors. Workplace Health and Safety, ethics and compliance are integral to these roles. You will undertake compliance checks, identify and report hazards and incidents, and contribute to risk assessments, audits, training and continuous improvement of safe work practices. SELECTION CRITERIA In addition to the Key Requirements for Success outlined in the Role Profile, the successful applicant must have: Demonstrated practical experience in anatomical techniques, which may include embalming, dissection, prosection, and familiarity with specialised equipment used within anatomy and pathology facilities. Ability and willingness to safely undertake the inherent physical requirements of the position, including manual handling associated with anatomical specimens, equipment and laboratory operations. Hepatitis B vaccination with demonstrated serology is mandatory to work within our Human Anatomy laboratories. Demonstrated willingness to acquire QFever vaccination, and to obtain other role-specific vaccinations where required with reasonable notice. It is a requirement of this position to hold and maintain a current C Class Queensland driver’s license; First Aid and CPR certification and a Current Working with Children Blue Card. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services on our Townsville campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your interest in Human Anatomy, Veterinary Anatomy and Pathology, or both. As well as your relevant experience in relation to the (1) key requirements for success as outlined in the role profile and (2) the selection criteria listed in this advertisement, outlining how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Dr Amanda Norton at Amanda.norton1@jcu.edu.au Applications close Tuesday, 17 November 2026 at 11:55pm. ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Technical Officer (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your laboratory and technical skills to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality learning and teaching across human and veterinary anatomy and pathology. Senior Lecturer, Adult Health Townsville Academic Bring your surgical expertise and passion for medical education to JCU, where you’ll shape clinical learning, inspire future doctors and strengthen healthcare across regional Australia. Clinical Educator / Lecturer, Occupational Therapy Townsville Academic Combine your passion for occupational therapy and clinical education in a rewarding role where you’ll shape the next generation of OTs while making a meaningful difference for children, young people and families in North Queensland. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.jcu.edu.au/jobs/senior-technical-advisor-education-life-and-environmental-sciences-cairns-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences)",
      "description": "Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) - Cairns, QLD, Australia Current Opportunities Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) 496133 Cairns Professional Technical Full time Closing on: Nov 17 2026 Position Description James Cook University (JCU) is creating a brighter future for life in the Tropics and beyond, through education and research that makes a difference locally and globally. Are you an experienced technical professional with expertise in biological sciences, laboratory operations or technical service environments? Join JCU in Cairns and play a key role in delivering safe, high-quality practical learning and teaching across Education, Life and Environmental Sciences in Cairns. We are seeking a capable and experienced Senior Technical Advisor to provide campus coordination, advanced technical advice, hands-on delivery support of practical learning activities across laboratory and technical service environments. Laboratory and Technical Services, Education Division Full-time, continuing | 36.25 hours per week Successful candidate must be based in Cairns or willing to relocate before commencement Based at the Cairns Nguma-bada campus, gateway to the Great Barrier Reef and tropical North Queensland HEWL 7: $99,878.44 - $110,446.52 per annum plus up to 17% superannuation ABOUT THE ROLE As the Senior Technical Advisor (Education, Life and Environmental Sciences) , you will coordinate and deliver high-quality technical services supporting practical learning and teaching activities. The portfolio spans practical teaching delivery across Education, Earth and Environmental Sciences, and Zoology and Ecology disciplines. The role also contributes to the effective delivery of Laboratory and Technical Services by the Education, Life and Environmental Sciences team in Cairns, by providing technical leadership and on-the-job guidance, building staff capability and supporting effective local work and campus coordination. You will coordinate key safety and compliance activities, including risk assessments, audits, inspections, incident and hazard reporting, training and safe work procedures, while providing high-level technical and operational advice to support service planning, quality assurance, problem-solving and continuous improvement. WHAT YOU WILL BRING TO THE ROLE You will bring relevant qualifications and advanced technical experience gained in complex biological, earth and/or environmental science laboratories, or similar technical service environments, ideally in a higher education environment. You will bring a demonstrated ability to train, guide and support others, with a sound understanding of Workplace Health and Safety requirements and experience in risk management and safe work practices. Your strong organisational, problem-solving and communication skills will enable you to manage competing priorities, exercise sound judgement and build effective working relationships. SELECTION CRITERIA In addition to the Key Requirements for Success outlined in the Role Profile, the successful applicant must have: Advanced technical experience within biological, earth and/or environmental science laboratories, or related scientific and technical environments, with demonstrated ability to coordinate and support the safe and effective delivery of practical learning and teaching activities across diverse disciplines. Demonstrated experience providing day-to-day technical leadership and operational coordination, including guiding and supporting technical staff, coordinating local work and campus priorities, providing on-the-job training and contributing to staff capability development. Significant experience coordinating laboratory and technical operations, including oversight of the operational readiness of specialised laboratories, equipment and instrumentation, and the coordination of facilities, resources and practical activities to support teaching and service requirements. Demonstrated experience coordinating safety and compliance activities within laboratory and technical environments, with sound knowledge of WHS requirements, risk management, chemical and biological safety, dangerous goods, scheduled medicines and positions, Australian laboratory standards and related regulatory requirements. Demonstrated ability to coordinate competing technical and operational requirements with advanced communication skills, and strong organisational and problem-solving skills, including the ability to exercise judgement and initiative, provide high-level technical advice, and support consistent service delivery in a complex multidisciplinary environment. It is a requirement of this position to hold and maintain a current C Class Queensland driver’s license, First Aid and CPR certification and a Working with Children Blue Card. WHY JCU JCU offers a dynamic and culturally diverse workplace where your ideas are valued, your professional growth is supported, and your work-life balance is respected. Working under the values of Authenticity , Excellence , Integrity , and Respect , we support and empower our people through the provisions of; A generous superannuation scheme with up to 17% employer contributions with UniSuper 5 weeks of annual recreation leave plus leave loading 15 days paid sick/carers leave per year Up to 6 months paid parental leave A range of flexible working options Staff study assistance and paid study leave Ongoing professional development support Fitness Passport Corporate discount on health insurance Free Employee Assistance Program (coaching and counselling) Well-equipped modern facilities and contemporary workspaces with access to on-site childcare and medical services at our Cairns’ campus HOW TO APPLY Are you ready to make a difference? Join us at JCU, where your future meets the tropics. Click the ‘apply’ button to be redirected to the JCU careers page , create an applicant account and follow the steps below: Complete the application form. Upload your current resume. Upload a cover letter outlining your relevant experience in relation to the (1) key requirements for success as outlined in the role profile and (2) the selection criteria listed in this advertisement, outlining how your skills and experience will ensure your success in the role. For any enquiries about the role, please contact Dr Amanda Norton at Amanda.norton1@jcu.edu.au Applications close Tuesday, 17 November 2026 at 11:55pm. ABOUT OUR PROCESS At JCU, we are committed to employing individuals who meet the requirements of the role and align with our values. All applicants will be contacted and advised of an outcome once the recruitment process is finalised. Please visit our Information Privacy Policy to understand how your information is collected, stored, accessed and used. James Cook University encourages people from all backgrounds who meet the role requirements to apply. We value and celebrate the diversity of our community and are committed to providing a safe, inclusive and welcoming learning and working environment. Recommended for you Technical Officer (Anatomy and Pathology) Townsville Professional, Technical Bring your laboratory and technical skills to JCU, supporting safe, high-quality learning and teaching across human and veterinary anatomy and pathology. Senior Lecturer, Adult Health Townsville Academic Bring your surgical expertise and passion for medical education to JCU, where you’ll shape clinical learning, inspire future doctors and strengthen healthcare across regional Australia. Clinical Educator / Lecturer, Occupational Therapy Townsville Academic Combine your passion for occupational therapy and clinical education in a rewarding role where you’ll shape the next generation of OTs while making a meaningful difference for children, young people and families in North Queensland. Facebook Twitter LinkedIn © James Cook University 1995 to 2026 | Cookie Preferences Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
